  "notes": "Power: none of these copper ports accepts PoE. Vendor page https://techspecs.ui.com/unifi/cloud-gateways/udw (HTTP 200, 704,702 B, read 2026-11-19, server-rendered tech-spec table) says \"Power Method = Universal AC input 100-240V AC, 7A Max., 50/60 Hz\"; a box fed from mains, a USB-C supply or a DC jack has no PoE-PD front end, so eth12 / eth13 / eth14 / eth15 / eth16 / eth17 now declare poeIn: false. Without that declaration the engine's isPoePd() match on \"unifi\" gave each silent copper port a 12.95 W 802.3af draw - the defect PR #2118 and PR #2121 fixed across the UXG family (refs #130)."
